==Battleground==
*1 [[Li'l Zyclone]] spawns after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>.
*2 [[Mesocosmocyclone]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] spawns as the boss.
**8 [[Mesocosmocyclone]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**5 [[Mesocosmocyclone]]s spawn, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
**5 [[Li'l Zyclone]]s spawn, delay 20~23.33 seconds<sup>600f~700f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Units such as [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] and [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] are good choices for crowd-controlling the Mesocosmocyclones while [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can]] can chip away at them. Once the boss appears, attack the Mesocosmocyclones with the aforementioned units and any other [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Aliens]] after luring them towards the base. [[Ancient Egg: N108 (Super Rare Cat)|Soap Cat]] is admittedly also useful here despite their lack of [[Immune to Warp|Warp Immunity]] as they can stall the Galactic Overseer Nyandam between Mesocosmocyclone waves, while also forcing the Li'l Zyclones to prematurely burrow. Do keep in mind that the Soap Cats will inevitably be warped beyond the enemy base and vanish forever. [[Ancient Egg: N107 (Rare Cat)|Cat Chief]] or [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] can deal with the Li'l Zyclones inflated HP pools. On higher magnifications, [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] can cause Explosions which shred through the horde pretty efficiently.

